[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; THE TOWN. Almost everything in it is built in code by World.gd (house style), so
; this scene is deliberately two nodes: the world script and the one body you drive.
;
; THE PLAYER BODY LEFT TOO, and that is the newest change: the town spawns a HERO
; now (`World._spawn_hero_body`) so you can cast in the lobby, and a body that needs a
; faction and a group at spawn cannot be parked in a scene file. This scene is one
; node — the script that builds everything.
;
; WHAT LEFT BEFORE THAT: the TileMapLayer (a retired top-down grass grid, invisible for
; months), two hard-coded NPC instances (the town's cast is now World.TOWNSFOLK, one
; editable list instead of a scene diff), and three RoomZone Area2Ds. The zones wrote
; `current_room_id` onto whoever walked through them, which existed for one thing: the
; LLM stack's "who is in earshot of a broadcast" test. That stack is deleted, so the
; zones and RoomZone.gd went with it rather than being left as a system with no reader.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://scripts/World.gd" id="2_world_script"]

[node name="Main" type="Node2D"]
script = ExtResource("2_world_script")
